# Clatter manual-mode patterns.
# Copy this file to  ~/.claude/clatter/manual-patterns  and add one shell glob per line
# (# starts a comment). Any session whose CWD matches a glob registers in MANUAL mode: peers can
# see it in `/clat peers`, but the relay will NEVER type /clat recv into it — no other session can
# drive a turn there. Use it for sensitive workspaces (EMR, legal, secrets).
#
# READ THIS:
#   Match your ACTUAL directory names, not the category. The globs are matched against a session's
#   cwd, so `*emr*` only helps if your EMR work literally lives in a path containing "emr". If your
#   sensitive dirs are ~/workspace/acme and ~/workspace/zephyr, you need *acme* and *zephyr* — `*emr*`
#   and `*legal*` would match NOTHING and silently protect nothing.
#
#   The guard fails OPEN: a glob that matches nothing looks identical to a working one. After editing
#   this file, run `clat doctor` to see exactly what it matches. A session's mode is fixed when it
#   registers, so restart (or re-register) a session after editing this file.
#
# Examples (replace with YOUR real directory names):
# *acme*
# *zephyr*
# */clients/*
# */.secrets/*
